# Shell scripts must check out with LF endings on every platform, including Windows.
#
# The scripts under quant-lab/ and scripts/ are not run on the machine that clones them -
# they are pushed to an Android device and executed by its /system/bin/sh, which treats a
# trailing carriage return as part of the command and fails on the first line. A judge
# cloning this repository on Windows with the default core.autocrlf would otherwise get
# CRLF copies that cannot run, and the failure reads as a broken script rather than a line
# ending.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Raw measurement outputs are compared byte for byte - by cmp in the judge guide, and by
# stage-equivalence.sh when it decides whether two arms agree. Rewriting their line endings
# on checkout would make a file differ from the one that was measured, which is the one
# thing this evidence cannot afford.
quant-lab/results/** -text
